# Project-root ./.env is AUTO-GENERATED by `make ensure-env` — it is decrypted
# from the checked-in, encrypted ./.env.dev (which holds the shared team
# NGROK_AUTHTOKEN). You normally do NOT edit ./.env by hand; docker compose
# reads it automatically for variable interpolation.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Setup: put the dotenvx private key in your shell (ask a teammate for the
# value), then `make up` / `make ios` just work — nothing to fill in here.
#
#   export DOTENV_PRIVATE_KEY_DEV=...        # add to ~/.zshrc
#
# That one env var decrypts ./.env.dev, pinai-agents/.env.dev and
# ops/litellm/.env.dev. (A <dir>/.env.keys file is the fallback if you'd
# rather not use an env var.)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Everything else is automatic per worktree:
#   - COMPOSE_PROJECT_NAME = pinai-<hash of worktree path>  (isolated group)
#   - host ports are random          → see `make urls`
#   - the ngrok public URL is assigned at runtime and injected into
#     pinai-chat → see `make tunnel-up` / `make urls`
